                "senderName": "NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 17 at 1:00PM MST until November 17 at 6:00PM MST by NWS Flagstaff AZ",
                "description": "FFWFGZ\n\nThe National Weather Service in Flagstaff has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCoconino County in north central Arizona...\nYavapai County in west central Arizona...\n\n* Until 600 PM MST.\n\n* At 100 PM MST, River gages in Munds Canyon indicated over 3 feet of\nrises and levels were still rising. This water will the work\nthrough the Munds Park area and into Oak Creek this afternoon.\nFlash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar and river gage indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nnormally dry washes, urban areas, highways, streets and\nunderpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nSedona, Munds Park, Indian Gardens, Uptown Sedona, Red Rock State\nPark and Cathedral Rock.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nInterstate 17 between mile markers 318 and 323. State Route 179\nbetween mile markers 311 and 313. State Route 89A between mile\nmarkers 374 and 379.\n\nThis includes the following swimming holes...\nMidgely Bridge, Buddha Beach \"Red Rock Crossing\" and Crescent Moon\nRanch.\n\nThis includes the following creeks, washes and rivers...\nOak Creek, Turkey Creek and Dry Beaver Creek.",
                "instruction": "Flooding of washes and creeks will occur, some dirt roads will become\nmuddy and impassable. Paved roads and underpasses could become\nflooded as well.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
